cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use awesome-verified-agents in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "Awesome Verified Agents: a curated list of tools that produce evidence about AI agent behaviour"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/awesome-verified-agents"
url: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/awesome-verified-agents"
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - verification
  - attestation
  - guardrails
  - observability
  - awesome list
abstract: >-
  A curated list of projects that leave an inspectable artifact behind an AI agent's
  actions — runtime enforcement that decides before an action runs, tamper-evident
  records, output verification against sources, benchmarks, tracing, and
  self-assessment. The inclusion bar is a single question: what artifact does it
  leave that a human can inspect later? Tools that only steer generation are out of
  scope. Star counts and last-commit dates are a dated snapshot rather than live
  badges, and no performance claim is restated that the maintainers have not run.
